              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\n51AH,APPEAL\n\nU.S. District Court\nWestern District of Tennessee (Memphis)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 2:23-cr-20121-TLP All Defendants\n\nCase title: United States of America v. Grayson et al Date Filed: 06/29/2023\n\nOther court case number: 25-851 US Supreme Court Date Terminated: 10/31/2024\n\nAssigned to: Judge Thomas L. Parker\nAppeals court case number: 24-5988\n\nDefendant (1)\nAshley Grayson represented by Scott H. Palmer\nUSM # 67352-510 SCOTT H. PALMER, P.C.\nTERMINATED: 10/31/2024 15455 Dallas Parkway\nSuite 540\nAddison, TX 75001\n214-987-4100\nFax: 214-922-9900\nEmail: scott@palmerperlstein.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nClaiborne Hambrick Ferguson\nTHE CLAIBORNE FERGUSON LAW FIRM, P.A.\n294 Washington Avenue\nMemphis, TN 38103\n901-529-6400\nFax: 901-202-2053\nEmail: Claiborne@midsouthcriminaldefense.com\nTERMINATED: 10/02/2023\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nLeslie I. Ballin\nBALLIN BALLIN & FISHMAN\n200 Jefferson Ave.\nSte. 1250\nMemphis, TN 38103\n901-525-6278\nFax: 901-525-6294\nEmail: june@bbfpc.com\nTERMINATED: 11/06/2024\nDesignation: Retained\n\nMichael Levine\nSCOTT PALMER\n15455 Dallas PKWY\nSte 540\nDallas, TX 75001\n214-987-4100\nEmail: mp.levine@yahoo.com\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nRussell Turkel\nSCOTT H. PALMER, P.C.\n15455 Dallas Pkwy\nSte 540\nAddison, TX 75001\n214-987-4100\nFax: 214-922-9900\nEmail: russell@palmerperlstein.com\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nPending Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nNone\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:1958 RACKETEERING - MURDER Defendant sentenced to 120 MONTHS incarceration. Followed\n(1) by 3 YEARS Supervised Release. Standard/Mandatory\nconditions of supervised release. Additional conditions: mental\nhealth testing and treatment as directed; mental health testing\nand treatment, no contact directly or indirectly with D.H., S. H.,\nand P. T., MRT and DNA collection. Special assessment in the\namount of $100.\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nAssigned to: Judge Thomas L. Parker\n\nDefendant (2)\nJoshua Grayson represented by Michael Edwin Scholl\nTERMINATED: 04/04/2024 MICHAEL E. SCHOLL, ATTORNEY AT LAW\n253 Adams Ave\nMemphis, TN 38103\n901-529-8500\nFax: 901-524-1803\nEmail: mike@scholl-law-firm.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:1958 RACKETEERING - MURDER\nAcquitted by Jury\n(1)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\nPlaintiff\nUnited States of America represented by Patrick Neal Oldham\nUS ATTORNEY'S OFFICE\n167 N. Main St.\nSuite 800\nMemphis, TN 38103\n901-544-4231\nEmail: neal.oldham@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nBryce Phillips\nUNITED STATES ATTORNEY'S OFFICE\n167 N. Main St.\nSuite 800\nMemphis, TN 38103\n901-229-0241\nEmail: bryce.phillips@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n06/29/2023 1 INDICTMENT as to Ashley Grayson (1) count(s) 1, Joshua Grayson (2) count(s) 1. (cas) (Entered: 06/30/2023)\n06/29/2023 2 INDICTMENT (PENALTY COPY) as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Attachments: # 1 Notice of Penalties) (cas) (Entered:\n06/30/2023)\n07/07/2023 5 Arrest Warrant Returned Executed on 7/7/2023 as to Ashley Grayson. (tlh) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 6 Arrest Warrant Returned Executed on 7/7/2023 as to Joshua Grayson. (tlh) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 7 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham: Initial Appearance as to Ashley Grayson (1) and Joshua\nGrayson (2) held on 7/7/2023. Defendants in custody and present in the courtroom. The Court read the charges to the defendants and\nadvised them of their rights. Rule 5(f) addressed. Ashley Grayson to retain Claiborne Ferguson; Joshua Grayson to retain Michael Scholl.\nGovernment agrees to $10,000.00 unsecured bond - Orders setting conditions of release entered. Arraignment set for Wednesday,\n8/9/2023 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 6 - Memphis before Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham. (AUSA: N. Oldham, W. Cornejo)(Defense\nCounsel: C. Ferguson) (Tape #FTR/CR6) (tlh) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 8 ORDER RE: CRIMINAL RULE 5(f) as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. Pursuant to the Due Process Protections Act, the Court\nconfirms the obligation of the United States to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland, 373 U.S.\n83 (1963), and its progeny, and orders it to do so. Failing to do so in a timely manner may result in consequences, including, but not\nlimited to, exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings, or sanctions by the Court. Signed\nby Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham on 7/7/2023. (Pham, Tu) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 9 CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by Ashley Grayson. (tlh) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 11 ORDER Setting Conditions of Release as to Ashley Grayson (1); $10,000.00 unsecured. Signed by Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham\non 7/7/2023. (Pham, Tu) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/07/2023 13 ORDER Setting Conditions of Release as to Joshua Grayson (2); $10,000.00 unsecured. Signed by Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham\non 7/7/2023. (Pham, Tu) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n07/11/2023 14 Surrender of Passport as to Ashley Grayson Passport Number 682835085 issued by USA (agj) (Entered: 07/11/2023)\n07/11/2023 15 Surrender of Passport as to Joshua Grayson Passport Number 560346489 issued by USA (agj) (Entered: 07/11/2023)\n07/12/2023 16 PRETRIAL SERVICES REPORT as to Ashley Grayson. (Walker, Michael) (Entered: 07/12/2023)\n07/12/2023 17 PRETRIAL SERVICES REPORT as to Joshua Grayson. (Henson, Christy) (Entered: 07/12/2023)\n07/27/2023 18 MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release to change residence to NC by Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Ferguson, Claiborne)\n(Entered: 07/27/2023)\n08/01/2023 19 ORDER [Text Only - No Image Attached] Granting 18 Motion to Modify Conditions of Release as to Ashley Grayson (1), Joshua Grayson\n(2). Signed by Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham on 8/1/2023. (Pham, Tu) (Entered: 08/01/2023)\n08/01/2023 20 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson: A Report Date/Scheduling Conference has been set for Wednesday, August 9,\n2023 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 6 - Memphis before Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham. (jrs) (Entered: 08/01/2023)\n08/02/2023 21 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Claiborne Hambrick Ferguson appearing for Ashley Grayson (Ferguson, Claiborne) (Entered:\n08/02/2023)\n08/02/2023 22 MOTION for Discovery by Ashley Grayson. (Ferguson, Claiborne) (Entered: 08/02/2023)\n08/03/2023 23 MOTION Waiver of Appearance at Arraignment by Ashley Grayson. (Ferguson, Claiborne) (Entered: 08/03/2023)\n08/07/2023 24 MOTION Waive Defendant's Appearance at Arraignment , proposed Order submitted by Joshua Grayson. (Attachments: # 1 Affidavit)\n(Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 08/07/2023)\n08/07/2023 25 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Michael Edwin Scholl appearing for Joshua Grayson (Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 08/07/2023)\n08/07/2023 26 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by Joshua Grayson (Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 08/07/2023)\n08/08/2023 27 ORDER [Text Only - No Image Attached] Granting 23 Motion to Waive Defendant's Appearance at Arraignment as to Ashley Grayson\n(1); Granting 24 Motion to Waive Defendant's Appearance at Arraignment as to Joshua Grayson (2). Signed by Chief Magistrate Judge Tu\nM. Pham on 8/8/2023. (Pham, Tu) (Entered: 08/08/2023)\n08/09/2023 28 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham: Arraignment as to Ashley Grayson (1) Count 1 and Joshua\nGrayson (2). Defendants appearance waived. Defendants were arraigned. Defendants, through counsel, waived formal reading of the\ncharges and entered a PLEA of NOT GUILTY on all counts. Trial Date and Report Date to be determined at following scheduling\nconference. (AUSA: N. Oldham)(Defense Counsel: C. Ferguson, M. Scholl) (Tape #FTR/CR6) (tlh) (Entered: 08/09/2023)\n08/09/2023 29 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham: Report Date/Scheduling Conference as to (1) Ashley\nGrayson and (2) Joshua Grayson held on 8/9/2023. Neal Oldham appeared for the government. Claiborne Ferguson appeared for (1)\nAshley Grayson; Michael Scholl appeared for (2) Joshua Grayson. The Court previously granted the defendants' motion to waive\nappearance 27 . The Court reminded parties as to Brady and its implications for exculpatory discovery. Discovery will be made available\nno later than August 16, 2023. 22 Defendant's Motion for Discovery will be termed upon minute entry. Any Pretrial Motions, including\nmotions to suppress, will be due by the end of day on September 15, 2023. A Final Report Date is set for Monday, October 23, 2023 at\n9:30 AM before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla in courtroom 7 on the 9th floor of the Odell Horton Federal Building. Any Plea Agreement\nshould be submitted to the court by noon on October 18, 2023. A Jury Trial is set for Monday, November 13, 2023 at 9:30 AM before\nJudge Jon Phipps McCalla in a courtroom to be determined. The trial is expected to take 4 days. The period from August 9, 2023 through\nNovember 13, 2023 is excluded under 18 U.S.C. Section 3161(h)(7)(B)(iv) to serve the ends of justice, for reasons stated in open court,\nand to allow for defense preparation. Defendants will remain on bond under current bond conditions. (Court Reporter: #FTR/CR6) (jrs)\n(Entered: 08/09/2023)\n08/09/2023 30 SCHEDULING ORDER as to (1) Ashley Grayson and (2) Joshua Grayson. Signed by Chief Magistrate Judge Tu M. Pham on 8/9/2023.\n(jrs) (Entered: 08/09/2023)\n08/16/2023 31 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n08/16/2023)\n09/13/2023 32 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Motions (extend deadline) by Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Ferguson, Claiborne) (Entered:\n09/13/2023)\n09/14/2023 33 ***TEXT ORDER (No Image Attached) GRANTING 32 Defendant's Joint Motion for Extension of Time to File as to Ashley Grayson\nand Joshua Grayson (1). For good cause shown, and without objection, the motion is hereby Granted and the pretrial motions deadline\nextended to September 28, 2023. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 9/14/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 09/14/2023)\n09/28/2023 34 MOTION for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice (Filing fee $ 150 receipt number ATNWDC-4246116) by Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: # 1\nGood Standing certificate)(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 09/28/2023)\n09/28/2023 35 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Claiborne H. Ferguson. by Ashley Grayson. (Ferguson, Claiborne) (Entered: 09/28/2023)\n09/29/2023 36 DEFICIENCY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 34 MOTION for Leave to Appear\nPro Hac Vice (Filing fee $ 150 receipt number ATNWDC-4246116) filed by Ashley Grayson has been filed. However, the following\ndeficiency has been found: Filer failed to include the required TWO certificates of good standing. This motion will be termed pending\nresubmission of entire motion with the correct amount of certificates. This motion will be termed, pending correct submission. Please refer\nto the ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and Procedures. The filer has one business day to correct the deficiency. (jae) (Entered:\n09/29/2023)\n09/29/2023 37 COURTESY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 35 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney\nby Claiborne H. Ferguson. filed by Ashley Grayson has been filed. For future reference, please note Filer failed to include \"proposed order\nsubmitted\" in docket text. Filer also failed to include a certificate of consultation. If no order previously email to chambers, please do so\nupon receipt of this notice. Please refer to the ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and Procedures. Filer is not required to resubmit\ndocument. (jae) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n09/29/2023 38 MOTION for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice (Fee paid as part of previous filing) by Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: # 1 Certificate of\nGood Standing, # 2 Certificate of Good Standing)(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n09/29/2023 39 ORDER GRANTING 38 Motion for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice as to Ashley Grayson (1). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n9/29/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n09/29/2023 40 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Scott H. Palmer appearing for Ashley Grayson (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n10/02/2023 41 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Leslie I. Ballin appearing for Ashley Grayson (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 10/02/2023)\n10/02/2023 42 ORDER Granting 35 Motion to Withdraw as Attorney. Upon Motion of the Defendant for permission to withdraw from this case, the\nCourt finds good cause shown and allows Claiborne H. Ferguson to withdraw from further representation of Ashley Grayson. Signed by\nJudge Jon Phipps McCalla on 10/2/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/02/2023)\n10/03/2023 43 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by Ashley Grayson (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n10/03/2023 44 MOTION for Extension of Time to File proposed Order submitted by Ashley Grayson. (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n10/03/2023 45 ORDER GRANTING 44 Defense Motion for Extension of Time to File as to Ashley Grayson (1). It appearing to the Court for good cause\nshown that the Motion is well taken and should be granted. The deadline for filing of pretrial motions is extended to November 15, 2023.\nSigned by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 10/3/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n10/05/2023 46 MOTION to Strike proposed Order submitted by Ashley Grayson. (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 10/05/2023)\n10/06/2023 47 ***TEXT ORDER***GRANTING 46 Defense Motion to Strike as to Ashley Grayson (1)and SETTING a Scheduling/Status Conference\nfor Friday, October 13, 2023 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 4 on the 9th floor of the Odell Horton Federal Building. Signed by Judge Jon\nPhipps McCalla on 10/6/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/06/2023)\n10/06/2023 48 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson: A Scheduling/Status Conference has been set for Friday, October 13,\n2023 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 4 - Memphis before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla. (jrs) (Entered: 10/06/2023)\n10/06/2023 49 MOTION to Continue Status/Scheduling Conference by Joshua Grayson. (Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 10/06/2023)\n10/09/2023 50 MOTION to Continue proposed order submitted by Ashley Grayson. (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 10/09/2023)\n10/10/2023 51 ORDER GRANTING 49 Defendant's Motion to Continue as to Joshua Grayson (2). For good cause shown, the Court hereby grants the\nmotion to continue the scheduling/status conference. The scheduling/status conference is reset to Thursday, October 26, 2023 at 9:30 AM\nin courtroom 7. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 10/10/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/10/2023)\n10/10/2023 52 ORDER GRANTING 50 Defendant's Motion to Continue as to Ashley Grayson (1). It is therefore ORDERED that the Scheduling\nConference/Report Date be and is reset to Thursday, October 26, 2023 at 9:30 AM before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla in courtroom 7 on the\n9th floor of the Odell Horton Federal Building. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 10/10/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/10/2023)\n10/10/2023 53 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson: The Scheduling/Status Conference has been RESET to THURSDAY,\nOCTOBER 26, 2023 at 9:30 AM in Courtroom 7 - Memphis before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla. (jrs) (Entered: 10/10/2023)\n10/12/2023 54 WAIVER of Personal Appearance at Arraignment and Entry of Plea of Not Guilty by Ashley Grayson (Palmer, Scott) (Entered:\n10/12/2023)\n10/13/2023 55 ORDER as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. Upon consideration, Defendant's motion 54 is hereby DENIED. The defendants are\nORDERED to appear in person for the Scheduling/Status Conference set for THURSDAY, OCTOBER 26, 2023 at 9:30 AM in courtroom\n7 on the 9th floor of the Odell Horton Federal Building in Memphis, Tennessee. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 10/13/2023. (jrs)\n(Entered: 10/13/2023)\n10/13/2023 56 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n10/13/2023)\n10/26/2023 57 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Report Date/Scheduling Conference as to Ashley Grayson (1) and\nJoshua Grayson (2) held on 10/26/2023. Neal Oldham appeared for the government. Leslie Ballin appeared for Ashley Grayson as Scott\nPalmer, co-counsel, is in trial in Plano, TX; Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson. Case information reviewed for the Court. No\nexperts are anticipated. Discovery is complete. Further electronic data will be submitted no later than November 2, 2023. Pretrial Motions,\nincluding any motions to suppress, should be filed by November 15, 2023. Expert reports will be due no later than November 30, 2023.\nAny Plea Agreement should be submitted to the court by noon on February 14, 2024. A Final Report Date is set for Friday, February 16,\n2024 at 9:30 AM in courtroom 7. The Jury Trial is reset to Monday, March 4, 2024 at 9:30 am in a courtroom to be determined. The trial is\nexpected to take 4 days. The Court granted defense oral Motion re: Speedy Trial clock. The period from October 26, 2023 through March\n4, 2024 is excluded under 18 U.S.C. Section 3161(h)(7)(B)(iv) in order to allow additional time to prepare for trial or under the following\nspecified provision: defense availability and preparation. Defendants to remain on bond under current bond conditions. (Court Reporter:\nTina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered: 10/26/2023)\n10/27/2023 58 AMENDED SCHEDULING ORDER as to Ashley Grayson (1) and Joshua Grayson (2). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n10/27/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 10/27/2023)\n11/02/2023 59 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n11/02/2023)\n11/08/2023 60 NOTICE OF FILING OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson held on October 26, 2023, before Judge Jon\nP. McCalla. Court Reporter Tina DuBose Gibson, Telephone number (901) 495-1538. Tape Number: None.\n\nNotice is hereby given that an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of the attorneys and pro se litigants who attended the hearing to which the\ntranscription applies. Each party is responsible for reviewing and requesting redaction of testimony of witnesses that were called for the\nparty and for that party's own statements.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from the court reporter or view the\ndocument at the clerk's office public terminal. Notice of Intent to Request Redaction due 11/13/2023. Redaction Request due 11/29/2023.\nRelease of Transcript Restriction set for 2/6/2024. (tdg) (Entered: 11/08/2023)\n11/15/2023 61 Sealed Document Motion In Limine and Memorandum in Support as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) Modified on 11/16/2023 to\nchange event type to Sealed Motion. (jae). (Entered: 11/15/2023)\n11/15/2023 62 Sealed Document Amended Motion in Limine and Memorandum In Support as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) Modified on 11/16/2023\nto change event type to Motion (jae). (Entered: 11/15/2023)\n11/15/2023 63 Sealed Document Motion to Exclude Evidence and Memorandum of Law In Support as to Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: # 1 Affidavit\nDeclaration of Amanda Fields, # 2 Exhibit ATF Report, # 3 Exhibit Johnson Phone Excerpts)(Palmer, Scott) Modified on 11/16/2023 to\nchange event type to \"motion\" (jae). (Entered: 11/15/2023)\n11/16/2023 64 COURTESY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 62 SEALED MOTION, 61 SEALED\nMOTION, 63 SEALED MOTION has been filed. For future reference, please note Filer should have selected the event \"Sealed Motion\"\nso that these would appear on the motion report for this case. Clerk's office has changed the event type to \"Sealed Motion\". Please refer to\nthe ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and Procedures. Filer is not required to resubmit document. (jae) (Entered: 11/16/2023)\n11/20/2023 65 MOTION for Extension of Time to File EXPERT WITNESS DESIGNATION AND REPORT DISCLOSURE DATE by Ashley Grayson.\n(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 11/20/2023)\n11/21/2023 66 Order GRANTING 65 Motion for Extension of Time to File as to Ashley Grayson (1). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n11/21/2023. (eoc) (Entered: 11/21/2023)\n11/28/2023 67 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Bryce Phillips appearing for USA. (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered: 11/28/2023)\n11/28/2023 68 First MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply proposed order submitted by United States of America as to Ashley\nGrayson, Joshua Grayson. (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered: 11/28/2023)\n11/29/2023 69 ORDER Granting 68 United States' Motion for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to Ashley Grayson (1). Upon motion of the\nUnited States, and for good cause shown, it is hereby ordered that the plaintiff's motion for extension of time is herby GRANTED. It is\nfurther ORDERED that the United States' response to the Defendants motion shall be filed on or before December 13, 2023. Signed by\nJudge Jon Phipps McCalla on 11/29/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 11/29/2023)\n12/12/2023 70 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to 63 SEALED MOTION proposed order submitted by United States of\nAmerica as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered: 12/12/2023)\n12/15/2023 71 ORDER Granting 70 United States' Motion for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to Ashley Grayson (1), Joshua Grayson (2).\nIt is hereby ordered that the plaintiff's motion for extension of time is herby GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that the United States'\nresponse to the Defendant's motion shall be filed on or before December 27, 2023. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 12/15/2023.\n(jrs) (Entered: 12/15/2023)\n12/15/2023 72 MOTION to Continue EXPERT WITNESS DESIGNATION AND REPORT DISCLOSURE DATE by Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott)\n(Entered: 12/15/2023)\n12/18/2023 73 ORDER GRANTING 72 Defense Motion to Continue as to Ashley Grayson (1). Came to be considered Defendant Ashley Grayson's\nUncontested Motion to Continue Expert Witness Designation and Report Disclosure Date. Upon consideration, the motion is hereby\nGRANTED. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 12/18/2023. (jrs) (Entered: 12/18/2023)\n12/18/2023 74 NOTICE of Expert Testimony by Ashley Grayson (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 12/18/2023)\n12/28/2023 75 SEALED RESPONSE to Motion re 63 SEALED MOTION (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered: 12/28/2023)\n01/04/2024 76 MOTION to Exclude to Join Co-Defendants Motion to Exclude Evidence and Memorandum of Law in Support by Joshua Grayson.\n(Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 01/04/2024)\n01/08/2024 77 Order GRANTING 76 Motion to Join Co-Defendant's Motion to Exclude Evidence and Memorandum in Support as to Joshua Grayson\n(2). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 01/08/2024. (eoc) (Entered: 01/08/2024)\n01/08/2024 78 Sealed Document ASHLEY GRAYSONS REPLY TO THE GOVERNMENTS RESPONSE TO DEFENDANTS MOTION TO EXCLUDE\nEVIDENCE as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 01/08/2024)\n01/19/2024 79 Sealed Document UNOPPOSED MOTION TO POSTPONE RULING ON DEFENDANTS MOTION TO EXCLUDE EVIDENCE as to\nAshley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 01/19/2024)\n01/22/2024 80 DEFICIENCY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 79 Sealed Document has been filed.\nHowever, the following deficiency has been found: Document must be resubmitted as a \"Sealed Motion\" in order for chambers to make a\nruling. Please refer to the ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and Procedures. The filer has one business day to correct the deficiency.\n(jae) (Entered: 01/22/2024)\n01/22/2024 81 Sealed Document SEALED UNOPPOSED MOTION TO POSTPONE RULING ON DEFENDANTS MOTION TO EXCLUDE EVIDENCE\nas to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 01/22/2024)\n01/23/2024 82 DEFICIENCY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 81 Sealed Document has been filed.\nHowever, the following deficiency has been found: Document must be resubmitted as a \"Sealed Motion\" in order for chambers to make a\nruling. Please refer to the ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and Procedures. The filer has one business day to correct the deficiency.\n(jae) (Entered: 01/23/2024)\n01/23/2024 83 SEALED MOTION TO POSTPONE RULING ON DEFENDANTS MOTION TO EXCLUDE EVIDENCE by Ashley Grayson. (Palmer,\nScott) (Entered: 01/23/2024)\n01/29/2024 85 TRANSCRIPT RELEASE NOTICE:\n\nBy Administrative Order 2008-35 the United States District Court for the Western District of Tennessee implemented a policy regarding\nremote access to electronic transcripts. Pursuant to that policy, as well as Civil Rule 5.2 and Criminal Rule 49.1, each party's attorney is\nrequired to review a transcript for information that should be redacted pursuant to the Judicial Conference's privacy policy which requires\nthat Social Security numbers be redacted to show only the last four digits; birth dates should contain only the year of birth; individuals\nknown to be minors should be referred to with initials; and financial account numbers should be redacted to the last four digits.\nAdditionally, in criminal case files, home addresses should reveal only the city and state of residence.\n\nOur records indicate that the 90-day restriction on public access to an electronic transcript(s) in this matter will lapse within 10 days. If a\nredaction request is required but has not been filed, please do so immediately. Please feel free to contact our office for further guidance on\nthis issue. (re: DE# 60 ; release date 2/6/2024) (tlh) (Entered: 01/29/2024)\n02/13/2024 86 Sealed Document NOTICE WITHDRAWING MOTION TO POSTPONE RULING ON DEFENDANTS MOTION TO EXCLUDE\nEVIDENCE as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 02/13/2024)\n02/15/2024 87 Order DENYING 61 62 First Motion in Limine and DENYING 63 Motion to Exclude. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n02/15/2024. (eoc) Modified on 1/13/2026 *UNSEALED PER ORDER 249 * (jae). (Main Document 87 replaced on 1/13/2026) (jae).\n(Main Document 87 replaced on 1/15/2026) (amm). (Main Document 87 replaced on 1/15/2026) (amm). (Main Document 87 replaced on\n1/15/2026) (amm). (Entered: 02/15/2024)\n02/16/2024 88 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: FinalReport Date as to Ashley Grayson (1) and Joshua Grayson (2)\nheld on 2/16/2024. Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government. Leslie Ballin and Scott Palmer appeared for Ashley\nGrayson (1); Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). The Court entered an order re: defendants Motions in Limine 87 .\nDiscovery is complete. There are no pending motions. The Court addressed the trial schedule in light of current trial schedules in other\ncourts. The Court Reset the Jury Trial to Monday, March 25, 2024 in a courtroom to be determined. The trial is expected to take 3 days.\nThe Court granted a Motions in Limine deadline of March 11, 2024; government response, if any, will be due by March 15, 2024. The\nCourt granted a new Plea Agreement deadline of March 13, 2024. The Court set a Final Report/COP for Monday, March 18, 2024 at 9:00\nAM in a courtroom to be determined with leave for defense to waive the final report if proceeding to trial. The Court Granted defense oral\nMotion as to time exclusion. Time is excluded from February 16, 2024 through March 25, 2024 to allow for the courts' trial schedules and\ncourtroom availability. Defendants will remain on bond under current bond conditions. (Court Reporter: Tina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered:\n02/16/2024)\n02/16/2024 89 AMENDED SCHEDULING ORDER as to Ashley Grayson (1) and Joshua Grayson (2). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n2/16/2024. (jrs) (Entered: 02/16/2024)\n03/07/2024 90 MOTION to Remove Report Date from Docket proposed Order submitted by Ashley Grayson. (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered: 03/07/2024)\n03/11/2024 91 ORDER GRANTING 90 Joint Motion to Remove Report Date from Docket. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 3/11/2024. (msr)\n(Entered: 03/11/2024)\n03/12/2024 92 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered:\n03/12/2024)\n03/15/2024 93 Rule 16 Discovery Request/Response by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n03/15/2024)\n03/15/2024 94 ORDER DIRECTING CLERK'S OFFICE TO PAY FOR LUNCHES FOR JURY TRIAL. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on\n3/15/2024. (jrs) (Main Document 94 replaced on 3/15/2024) (jrs). (Entered: 03/15/2024)\n03/18/2024 95 RELEASE STATUS REPORT as to Ashley Grayson. (Walker, Michael) (Entered: 03/18/2024)\n03/18/2024 96 RELEASE STATUS REPORT as to Joshua Grayson. (Henson, Christy) (Entered: 03/18/2024)\n03/18/2024 98 MOTION for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice (Filing fee $ 150 receipt number ATNWDC-4368625) by Ashley Grayson. (Levine, Michael)\n(Entered: 03/18/2024)\n03/18/2024 99 DEFICIENCY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 98 MOTION for Leave to Appear\nPro Hac Vice (Filing fee $ 150 receipt number ATNWDC-4368625) filed by Ashley Grayson has been filed. However, the following\ndeficiency has been found: both certificates are from a US District Court, but our LR state one must be from the highest court of the state\nin which you are licensed to practice. This motion will be termed pending submission of correct certificates. Please refer to the ECF User\nManual and ECF Policies and Procedures. The filer has one business day to correct the deficiency. (jae) (Entered: 03/18/2024)\n03/18/2024 100 MOTION for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice proposed order submitted (Fee paid as part of previous filing) by Ashley Grayson. (Levine,\nMichael) (Entered: 03/18/2024)\n03/19/2024 101 Sealed Document Rule 16 Discovery Response as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 03/19/2024)\n03/20/2024 102 SEALED MOTION proposed order submitted by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Phillips, Bryce)\n(Entered: 03/20/2024)\n03/21/2024 103 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson: The JURY TRIAL is set for MONDAY, MARCH 25, 2024 at 9:30 AM in\nCourtroom 1 - Memphis before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla. (jrs) (Entered: 03/21/2024)\n03/21/2024 105 Order GRANTING 100 Motion for Leave to Appear Pro Hac Vice (Levine). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla on 03/21/2024. (eoc)\n(Entered: 03/21/2024)\n03/21/2024 107 SEALED MOTION by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered: 03/21/2024)\n03/22/2024 108 Sealed Document Proposed Witness List and Order of Proof as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson. (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n03/22/2024)\n03/22/2024 109 Sealed Document Proposed Witness List as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 03/22/2024)\n03/22/2024 110 Sealed Document as to Joshua Grayson. (Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 03/22/2024)\n03/22/2024 111 Sealed Document Rule 16 Discovery Response as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 03/22/2024)\n03/22/2024 112 Sealed Document Response to Government's Motion in Limine to Exclude Evidence as to Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered:\n03/22/2024)\n03/24/2024 113 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Michael Levine appearing for Ashley Grayson (Levine, Michael) (Entered: 03/24/2024)\n03/25/2024 114 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Jury Trial as to Ashley Grayson (1), Joshua Grayson (2) held on\n3/25/2024 (DAY 1). Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government with Case Agent, Janelle Hosafros. Scott Palmer,\nMichael Levine, and Leslie Ballin appeared for Ashley Grayson (1). Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). Both defendants, on\nbond, were present in court. The Court reviewed preliminary matters, pending motion 107 , trial schedule or organization. Voir dire oath\nadministered. Jury selection begun. Parties dismissed for the day. Jury selection will resume tomorrow, Tuesday, March 26, 2024. Jury\npool will report to 11th floor at 8:30 AM. Attorneys will report no later than 8:20 AM. Matters concluded for the day. Defendants remain\non bond. (Court Reporter: Tina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered: 03/25/2024)\n03/26/2024 116 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Jury Trial as to Ashley Grayson (1), Joshua Grayson (2) held (Day\n2) on 3/26/2024. Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government with case agent, Janelle Hosafros. Scott Palmer, Michael\nLevine, and Leslie Ballin appeared for Ashley Grayson (1). Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). Both defendants, on bond,\nwere present in court. Order 115 entered in re: to 107 . Voir dire jury selection resumed. Jury selected and sworn: 12 jurors and 2\nalternatives seated. Preliminary jury instructions given. Opening statements given. Government's sworn witnesses/proof: Jenny Chung;\nExhibit 1; Olivia Johnson; Exhibit 2-10. Jury dismissed for the day. Jury and attorneys will report at 8:30 AM. Defendants remain on\nbond. (Court Reporter: Tina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered: 03/26/2024)\n03/26/2024 117 Jury List. (jrs) (Main Document 117 replaced on 3/27/2024) (jrs). (Entered: 03/26/2024)\n03/26/2024 118 Peremptory Challenges. (jrs) (Entered: 03/26/2024)\n03/26/2024 119 Jury Seating Arrangement. (jrs) (Entered: 03/26/2024)\n03/26/2024 120 NOTICE OF FILING OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT (Testimony of Olivia Johnson) as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson held on March\n26, 2024, before Judge Jon P. McCalla. Court Reporter Tina DuBose Gibson, Telephone number (901) 495-1538. Tape Number: None.\n\nNotice is hereby given that an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of the attorneys and pro se litigants who attended the hearing to which the\ntranscription applies. Each party is responsible for reviewing and requesting redaction of testimony of witnesses that were called for the\nparty and for that party's own statements.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from the court reporter or view the\ndocument at the clerk's office public terminal. Notice of Intent to Request Redaction due 4/1/2024. Redaction Request due 4/16/2024.\nRelease of Transcript Restriction set for 6/24/2024. (tdg) (Entered: 03/26/2024)\n03/27/2024 121 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Jury Trial as to Ashley Grayson (1), Joshua Grayson (2) held on\n3/27/2024 (DAY 3). Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government with case agent, Janelle Hosafros. Scott Palmer,\nMichael Levine, and Leslie Ballin appeared for Ashley Grayson (1). Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). Both defendants, on\nbond, were present in court. Preliminary matters addressed. Governments sworn witnesses/proof (continued): Olivia Johnson (resumed\ntestimony); Exhibits 11-21; Leslie Jones; Exhibits 22-23; Brandon Thomas; Janelle Hosafros; Exhibits 24-25. Jury dismissed for the day at\n5:12 pm. The Court reviewed with parties the anticipated trial schedule and jury instructions. The jury trial will resume on Thursday,\nMarch 27, 2024 at 8:45 AM. Jury will report no later than 8:30 AM. Attorneys will report by 8:15 AM. Defendants remain on bond. (Court\nReporter: Tina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered: 03/27/2024)\n03/28/2024 122 NOTICE OF FILING OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson held on March 26, 2024, before Judge Jon P.\nMcCalla. Court Reporter Tina DuBose Gibson, Telephone number 9014951538. Tape Number: None.\nNotice is hereby given that an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of the attorneys and pro se litigants who attended the hearing to which the\ntranscription applies. Each party is responsible for reviewing and requesting redaction of testimony of witnesses that were called for the\nparty and for that party's own statements.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from the court reporter or view the\ndocument at the clerk's office public terminal. Notice of Intent to Request Redaction due 4/2/2024. Redaction Request due 4/18/2024.\nRelease of Transcript Restriction set for 6/26/2024. (tdg) (Main Document 122 replaced on 4/5/2024) (cbs). (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n03/28/2024 123 JURY INSTRUCTIONS. (eoc) (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n03/28/2024 124 VERDICT FORM - ASHLEY GRAYSON. (eoc) (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n03/28/2024 125 VERDICT FORM - JOSHUA GRAYSON. (eoc) (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n03/28/2024 126 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Jury Trial as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson held on 3/28/2024\n(DAY 4). Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government with case agent, Janelle Hosafros. Scott Palmer, Michael Levine,\nand Leslie Ballin appeared for Ashley Grayson (1). Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). Both defendants, on bond, were\npresent in court. Preliminary matters addressed. Government's sworn witnesses/proof (continued): Janelle Hosafros (resumed testimony);\nExhibit 26; Derricka Harwell; Exhibits 27-38. Government rests. Defendant's Oral Motion for Acquittal (Rule 29, FRP) Denied. Outside\nthe presence of the jury, defendants Ashley Grayson and Joshua Grayson sworn and informed the Court they would not testify. The Court\nreviewed proposed jury instructions with attorneys outside the presence of the jury. Jury returned. Defendants rest. Outside the presence of\nthe jury, defense counsel's renewed oral Motion for Judgment of Acquittal (Rule 29) was Denied. Government and defense closing\narguments given. Government's rebuttal arguments given. Charge conference held. Jury charge/instructions given. Jury dismissed to begin\ndeliberations at 3:53 PM. Having not reached a verdict, the jury returned to court at 5:00 PM to be dismissed for the day. Jury\ndeliberations will resume Friday, March 29, 2024 at 8:30 AM. Attorneys will report to court at 11:55 am unless notified to return earlier.\nDefendants remain on bond. (Court Reporter: Lisa Mayo) (jrs) (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n03/29/2024 127 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla: Jury Trial as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson held on 3/29/2024\n(Day 5). Neal Oldham and Bryce Phillips appeared for the government with case agent, Janelle Hosafros. Scott Palmer and Michael\nLevine appeared for Ashley Grayson (1). Michael Scholl appeared for Joshua Grayson (2). Both defendants, on bond, were present in\ncourt. Jury resumed deliberation at 8:23 am. The Jury advised the court of a verdict and returned to court at 12:26 PM. Jury polled. As to\nAshley Grayson (1), the jury returned a Guilty Verdict (Count 1). As to Joshua Grayson (2), the jury returned a Not Guilty Verdict (Count\n1). Jury discharged at 12:44. Sentencing is set for Friday July 12, 2024 at 9:30 AM in a courtroom to be determined. The Court heard\narguments as to governments oral Motion re: bond revocation and custody for Ashley Grayson (1). The Court heard from Pretrial Services\nofficer Christy Henson. The Court outlined release conditions under which defendant, Ashley Grayson, would remain on bond. An Order\nmodifying bond conditions will be entered. Parties dismissed. (Court Reporter: Tina Gibson) (jrs) (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/29/2024 131 EXHIBIT AND WITNESS LIST FOR JURY TRIAL. (jrs) (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/29/2024 133 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson: Sentencing is set for Friday, July 12, 2024 at 9:30 AM in Courtroom 7 - Memphis before Judge\nJon Phipps McCalla. (jrs) (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n04/04/2024 134 JUDGMENT as to Joshua Grayson (2). A jury having been impaneled, the case having been tried, and a verdict of not guilty returned, IT\nIS THEREFORE ORDERED that the Defendant is acquitted, discharged, and any bond exonerated. Signed by Judge Jon Phipps McCalla\non 4/4/2024. (jrs) (Entered: 04/04/2024)\n04/10/2024 135 SEALED MOTION To Continue Sentencing Hearing by Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 04/10/2024)\n04/12/2024 137 SEALED MOTION for Acquittal or Alternatively a New Trial by Ashley Grayson. (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 04/12/2024)\n04/16/2024 138 SETTING LETTER as to Ashley Grayson: The SENTENCING HEARING before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla has been RESET to\nFRIDAY, AUGUST 16, 2024 at 9:30 A.M. in courtroom 7 on the 9th floor of the Odell Horton Federal Building. (jrs) (Entered:\n04/16/2024)\n04/26/2024 139 MOTION for Return of Property/PostTrial , proposed Order submitted by Joshua Grayson. (Scholl, Michael) (Entered: 04/26/2024)\n04/29/2024 140 ORDER GRANTING 139 Defense Motion for Return of Property/PostTrial as to Joshua Grayson (2). Signed by Judge Jon Phipps\nMcC