edia wish to attend in the video proceeding, please click on the\nfollowing link to request access information: https://www.tnwd.uscourts.gov/videohearings The access information will be delivered via\nemail to the email address from which the request originated.\n\nParties should consult the instructions for Joining a Meeting in Teams or Joining a Meeting Without a Teams Account.\n\nPlease email Sandra McClain at sandra_mcclain@tnwd.uscourts.gov for any questions. (smm) (Entered: 08/05/2024)\n08/06/2024 178 PRESENTENCE REPORT FINAL (Sealed) as to Ashley Grayson. NOTICE: Document is available to applicable parties only. Click on\ndocument number in this NEF; enter your PACER login and password when the login screen appears. Click View Document. Save or print\ndocument. There is only one view via the NEF. (Attachments: # 1 ADDENDUM, # 2 RECOMMENDATION) (Harford, Randal) (Entered:\n08/06/2024)\n08/06/2024 179 NOTICE OF CANCELLATION as to Ashley Grayson: The Status Conference currently set for Wednesday, August 14, 2024 at 2:00 PM.\nvia Microsoft Teams Video Conference before Judge Thomas L. Parker has been cancelled. The parties will receive the date of the next\nsetting by a separate entry. (smm) (Entered: 08/06/2024)\n08/06/2024 180 TEXT NOTICE SETTING STATUS CONFERENCE as to Ashley Grayson: (TEXT ONLY - NO IMAGE ASSOCIATED WITH THIS\nENTRY): The Court will hold a Status Conference in lieu of the Sentencing Hearing on Friday, August 16, 2024 at 9:30 A.M. in\nCourtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker.(smm) (Entered: 08/06/2024)\n08/08/2024 181 SEALED MOTION FOR LEAVE TO WAIVE PERSONAL APPEARANCE AT STATUS CONFERENCE (proposed order submitted) by\nAshley Grayson. (Turkel, Russell) (Entered: 08/08/2024)\n08/12/2024 183 TRANSCRIPT RELEASE NOTICE:\n\nBy Administrative Order 2008-35 the United States District Court for the Western District of Tennessee implemented a policy regarding\nremote access to electronic transcripts. Pursuant to that policy, as well as Civil Rule 5.2 and Criminal Rule 49.1, each party's attorney is\nrequired to review a transcript for information that should be redacted pursuant to the Judicial Conference's privacy policy which requires\nthat Social Security numbers be redacted to show only the last four digits; birth dates should contain only the year of birth; individuals\nknown to be minors should be referred to with initials; and financial account numbers should be redacted to the last four digits.\nAdditionally, in criminal case files, home addresses should reveal only the city and state of residence.\n\nOur records indicate that the 90-day restriction on public access to an electronic transcript(s) in this matter will lapse within 10 days. If a\nredaction request is required but has not been filed, please do so immediately. Please feel free to contact our office for further guidance on\nthis issue. (re: DE# 148 ; release date 8/21/2024) (tlh) (Entered: 08/12/2024)\n08/14/2024 184 Sealed Document Ashley Grayson's Objection to the Presentence Report Addendum as to Ashley Grayson. (Turkel, Russell) (Entered:\n08/14/2024)\n08/15/2024 185 Sealed Document United States Second Position on the PSR as to Ashley Grayson. (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered: 08/15/2024)\n08/15/2024 186 RELEASE STATUS REPORT as to Ashley Grayson. (Washington, Simone) (Entered: 08/15/2024)\n08/16/2024 187 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Thomas L. Parker as to Ashley Grayson: Status Conference as to Ashley Grayson was\nheld on 8/16/2024. Bryce Phillips and Neal Oldham appeared for the government. Leslie Ballin present in court for defendant. Scott H.\nPalmer and Russell Turkel appeared telephonically. Defendant Ashley Grayson on bond and appeared telephonically. The court discussed\nthe status of the case with the parties. A Sentencing Hearing has been set for Thursday, September 26, 2024 at 1:30 PM in Courtroom 2 -\nMemphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker. Defendant to remain on present bond. (Court Reporter: Catherine Phillips) (smm) (Entered:\n08/16/2024)\n08/16/2024 188 TEXT NOTICE SETTING SENTENCING HEARING as to Ashley Grayson: A Sentencing Hearing has been set for Thursday,\nSeptember 26, 2024 at 1:30 P.M. in Courtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker.\n\n*The parties are instructed to notify the case manager immediately if they anticipate an evidentiary hearing lasting over an hour.\n\nThe parties are also instructed to have present any witnesses who will be needed for this hearing.\n\n(smm) (Entered: 08/16/2024)\n08/23/2024 189 SEALED MOTION for Reconsideration of Denial of Motion for Mistrial (proposed order submitted) by Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: #\n1 Exhibit)(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/24/2024 190 Amended SEALED MOTION for Reconsideration of Denial of Motion for Mistrial (proposed order submitted) by Ashley Grayson.\n(Attachments: # 1 Exhibit)(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 08/24/2024)\n09/10/2024 191 [**TEXT ORDER TO SHOW CAUSE -- NO IMAGE ATTACHED**] ORDER TO SHOW CAUSE: On August 24, 2024, Defendant,\nAshley Grayson, moved to Reconsider the ruling on her earlier Motion for Mistrial. (ECF Nos. 189, 190.) Under LR 12.1, the opponent of\na motion has 14 days to respond. The Government has yet to Respond here and the time to do so has expired. The Government has until\nthe close of business on Monday, September 16, 2024, to Show Cause as to why the Court should not grant Defendants pending motion.\nSigned by Judge Thomas L. Parker on 9/10/2024. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 09/10/2024)\n09/11/2024 192 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply and Response to Show Cause Order by United States of America as to Ashley\nGrayson. (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered: 09/11/2024)\n09/11/2024 193 ORDER granting the United States' 192 Motion for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to Ashley Grayson (1). Signed by Judge\nThomas L. Parker on 9/11/2024. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 09/11/2024)\n09/18/2024 194 SUPPLEMENTAL PROBATION FILING-SECOND ADDENDUM TO