a the NEF. (Attachments: # 1 Victim\nLetters of Support) (Harford, Randal) (Entered: 09/25/2024)\n09/25/2024 204 TEXT NOTICE RE-SETTING SENTENCING HEARING as to Ashley Grayson: The Sentencing Hearing has been reset for Thursday,\nOctober 31, 2024 at 1:30 P.M. in Courtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker.\n\n*The parties are instructed to notify the case manager immediately if they anticipate an evidentiary hearing lasting over an hour.\n\nThe parties are also instructed to have present any witnesses who will be needed for this hearing.\n\n(smm) (Entered: 09/25/2024)\n10/08/2024 205 Sealed Document Ashley Grayson's Objection to the Presentence Report Third Addendum as to Ashley Grayson. (Turkel, Russell)\n(Entered: 10/08/2024)\n10/29/2024 207 SUPPLEMENTAL PROBATION FILING-FOURTH ADDENDUM TO PRESENTENCE REPORT as to Ashley Grayson. NOTICE:\nDocument is available to applicable parties only. Click on document number in this NEF; enter your PACER login and password when the\nlogin screen appears. Click View Document. Save or print document. There is only one view via the NEF. (Attachments: # 1 Victim\nLetters of Support) (Harford, Randal) (Entered: 10/29/2024)\n10/29/2024 208 Sealed Document Ashley Grayson's Objection to the Presentence Report Fourth Addendum as to Ashley Grayson. (Turkel, Russell)\n(Entered: 10/29/2024)\n10/29/2024 209 SEALED MOTION for Appellate Bond (proposed order submitted) by Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit Partial Appellate Brief)\n(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 10/29/2024)\n10/30/2024 210 SEALED RESPONSE to Motion re 209 SEALED MOTION for Appellate Bond (proposed order submitted) (Oldham, Patrick) (Entered:\n10/30/2024)\n10/31/2024 211 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Thomas L. Parker as to Ashley Grayson: Sentencing Hearing as Ashley Grayson was held\non 10/31/2024. Neal Oldham appeared for the government. Scott H. Palmer, Russell Turkel and Leslie Ballin appeared for the defense.\nDefendant on bond and present. Defendant was heretofore found guilty as to count 1 of the indictment on 3/28/2024. Defendant's exhibit 1\nmarked and admitted. Defendant sentenced to 120 MONTHS incarceration. Followed by 3 YEARS Supervised Release.\nStandard/Mandatory conditions of supervised release. Additional conditions: mental health testing and treatment as directed; mental health\ntesting and treatment, no contact directly or indirectly with D.H., S. H., and P. T., MRT and DNA collection. Special assessment in the\namount of $100. Defendant's Sealed Motion for Release Pending Appeal 209 was denied. The court recommends to the BOP: designation\nto Carswell Federal Medical Center in Fort Worth, Texas to be near family. The court advised defendant of appellate rights/Appeal packet\nhanded to defendant. Defendant to report as directed. (USPO: Vanessa Roberts) (Court Reporter: Catherine Phillips) (smm) (Entered:\n10/31/2024)\n10/31/2024 212 EXHIBIT LIST as to Ashley Grayson.(smm) (Main Document 212 replaced on 6/5/2026 to reflect correct exhibits) (smm). (Entered:\n10/31/2024)\n10/31/2024 213 JUDGMENT as to Ashley Grayson: Defendant sentenced to 120 MONTHS incarceration. Followed by 3 YEARS Supervised Release.\nStandard/Mandatory conditions of supervised release. Additional conditions: mental health testing and treatment as directed; mental health\ntesting and treatment, no contact directly or indirectly with D.H., S. H., and P. T., MRT and DNA collection. Special assessment in the\namount of $100. The court recommends to the BOP: designation to Carswell Federal Medical Center in Fort Worth, Texas to be near\nfamily. Signed by Judge Thomas L. Parker on 10/31/2024. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 10/31/2024)\n10/31/2024 214 REDACTED JUDGMENT as to Ashley Grayson: Defendant sentenced to 120 MONTHS incarceration. Followed by 3 YEARS\nSupervised Release. Standard/Mandatory conditions of supervised release. Additional conditions: mental health testing and treatment as\ndirected; mental health testing and treatment, no contact directly or indirectly with D.H., S. H., and P. T., MRT and DNA collection.\nSpecial assessment in the amount of $100. The court recommends to the BOP: designation to Carswell Federal Medical Center in Fort\nWorth, Texas to be near family. Signed by Judge Thomas L. Parker on 10/31/2024. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 10/31/2024)\n11/01/2024 215 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney proposed order submitted by Leslie I. Ballin. by Ashley Grayson. (Ballin, Leslie) (Entered:\n11/01/2024)\n11/01/2024 216 NOTICE OF APPEAL by Ashley Grayson re 213 Judgment,,. Filing fee $ 605, receipt number ATNWDC-4539897. (Palmer, Scott)\n(Entered: 11/01/2024)\n11/01/2024 217 USCA Case Number as to Ashley Grayson 24-5988 for 216 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment filed by Ashley Grayson. (mf) (Entered:\n11/04/2024)\n11/05/2024 218 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Ashley Grayson for proceedings held on 8/16/24, 10/31/24 before Judge Thomas L. Parker, re 216 Notice\nof Appeal - Final Judgment (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 11/05/2024)\n11/05/2024 219 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Ashley Grayson for proceedings held on 7/7/23, 8/9/23, 8/9/23 before Judge Tu M. Pham, re 216 Notice of\nAppeal - Final Judgment (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 11/05/2024)\n11/05/2024 220 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Ashley Grayson for proceedings held on 3/28/24 before Judge Jon Phipps McCalla, re 216 Notice of Appeal\n- Final Judgment (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 11/05/2024)\n11/05/2024 221 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Ashley Grayson for proceedings held on 10/26/23, 2/16/24, 3/25/25-3/27/24, 3/29/24 before Judge Jon\nPhipps McCalla, re 216 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 11/05/2024)\n11/06/2024 222 ORDER GRANTING Motion to Withdraw as Attorney 215 as to Ashley Grayson. Signed by Judge Thomas L. Parker on 11/06/2024.\n(Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 11/06/2024)\n11/15/2024 223 NOTIFICATION OF PRISONER DESIGNATION as to Ashley Grayson. (smm) (Entered: 11/15/2024)\n11/15/2024 224 ORDER TO SURRENDER as to Ashley Grayson. Defendant IS HEREBY ORDERED to surrender to the Bureau of Prisons by reporting\nto FMC Carswell, Naval Air Station, J Street, Fort Worth, Texas 76127 by 2:00 P.M. on THURSDAY, DECEMBER 19, 2024. Signed by\nJudge Thomas L. Parker on 11/15/2024. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 11/15/2024)\n11/26/2024 225 NOTICE OF FILING OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT as to Ashley Grayson held on July 7, 2023, before Judge Tu M. Pham. Court\nReporter Catherine Phillips (FTR RECORDING), Telephone number 901-495-1535.\n\nNotice is hereby given that an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of the attorneys and pro se litigants who attended the hearing to which the\ntranscription applies. Each party is responsible for reviewing and requesting redaction of testimony of witnesses that were called for the\nparty and for that party's own statements.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from the court reporter or view the\ndocument at the clerk's office public terminal. Notice of Intent to Request Redaction due 12/2/2024. Redaction Request due 12/17/2024.\nRelease of Transcript Restriction set for 2/24/2025. (cjp) (Entered: 11/26/2024)\n11/26/2024 226 NOTICE OF FILING OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT as to Ashley Grayson held on August 9, 2023, before Judge Tu M. Pham. Court\nReporter Catherine Phillips (FTR RECORDING), Telephone number 901-495-1535.\n\nNotice is hereby given that an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of