hat an official transcript of a proceeding has been filed by the court reporter in this matter. The parties have seven\n(7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript, and twenty-one (21) calendar days to file\na Request for Redaction. Redaction is the responsibility of the attorneys and pro se litigants who attended the hearing to which the\ntranscription applies. Each party is responsible for reviewing and requesting redaction of testimony of witnesses that were called for the\nparty and for that party's own statements.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from the court reporter or view the\ndocument at the clerk's office public terminal. Notice of Intent to Request Redaction due 12/2/2024. Redaction Request due 12/17/2024.\nRelease of Transcript Restriction set for 2/24/2025. (cjp) (Entered: 11/26/2024)\n12/06/2024 229 ORDER of USCA (certified copy) as to Ashley Grayson re 216 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment (mf) (Entered: 12/06/2024)\n02/04/2025 230 Letter from Ian Frisch as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson requesting for Indictment, any and all exhibits, and any and all pre-trial and\ntrial transcripts to be unsealed. (Attachments: # 1 Envelope) (cmm) (Entered: 02/05/2025)\n02/12/2025 231 NOTICE of Filing of Trial Exhibits by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit Trial Exhibit 5:\nExtraction Report Apple iPhone)(Oldham, Patrick) (Entered: 02/12/2025)\n02/18/2025 232 TRANSCRIPT RELEASE NOTICE:\n\nBy Administrative Order 2008-35 the United States District Court for the Western District of Tennessee implemented a policy regarding\nremote access to electronic transcripts. Pursuant to that policy, as well as Civil Rule 5.2 and Criminal Rule 49.1, each party's attorney is\nrequired to review a transcript for information that should be redacted pursuant to the Judicial Conference's privacy policy which requires\nthat Social Security numbers be redacted to show only the last four digits; birth dates should contain only the year of birth; individuals\nknown to be minors should be referred to with initials; and financial account numbers should be redacted to the last four digits.\nAdditionally, in criminal case files, home addresses should reveal only the city and state of residence.\n\nOur records indicate that the 90-day restriction on public access to an electronic transcript(s) in this matter will lapse within 10 days. If a\nredaction request is required but has not been filed, please do so immediately. Please feel free to contact our office for further guidance on\nthis issue. (re: DE# 225 , DE# 226 , DE# 227 , DE# 228 ; release date 2/24/2025) (tlh) (Entered: 02/18/2025)\n02/18/2025 233 Transcript Redaction Request in case as to Ashley Grayson re 145 Transcript,,,, 147 Transcript,,,, 144 Transcript,,,, filed by attorney Scott\nH. Palmer (Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 02/18/2025)\n02/26/2025 234 MOTION to Redact 145 Transcript,,,, 147 Transcript,,,, 144 Transcript,,,, propsed order submitted by Ashley Grayson. (Attachments: # 1\nProposed Order)(Palmer, Scott) (Entered: 02/26/2025)\n02/26/2025 235 ORDER GRANTING DEFENDANT ASHLEY GRAYSON'S MOTION TO REDACT TRANSCRIPTS 234 . Signed by Judge Thomas L.\nParker on 2/26/2025. (Parker, Thomas) (Entered: 02/26/2025)\n03/06/2025 236 Redaction re 144 Trial Transcript,,,, in case as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (tdg) (Entered: 03/06/2025)\n03/06/2025 237 Redaction re 145 Trial Transcript,,,, in case as to Ashley Grayson, Joshua Grayson (tdg) (Entered: 03/06/2025)\n03/12/2025 238 TEXT NOTICE SETTING STATUS CONFERENCE as to Ashley Grayson: (TEXT ONLY - NO IMAGE ASSOCIATED WITH THIS\nENTRY): A Status Conference, to discuss the \"restricted status\" of the case, has been set for Wednesday, March 19, 2025 at 1:30 P.M. in\nCourtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker. This hearing is for attorneys only, the defendant's presence is not required.(smm)\n(Entered: 03/12/2025)\n03/18/2025 239 TEXT NOTICE RE-SETTING STATUS CONFERENCE as to Ashley Grayson: (TEXT ONLY - NO IMAGE ASSOCIATED WITH\nTHIS ENTRY): The Status Conference, to discuss the \"restricted status\" of the case, has been reset for Thursday, March 27, 2025 at\n1:30 P.M. in Courtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker. This hearing is for attorneys only, the defendant's presence is not\nrequired.(smm) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/20/2025 240 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Thomas L. Parker as to Ashley Grayson: A Telephonic Status Conference, to discuss the\nrestricted status of the case was held on 3/20/2025. Bryce Phillips appeared for the government. Scott H. Palmer, Russell Turkel and Niles\nIllich appeared for the defense. Defendant's presence is waived for this hearing. After hearing argument from both sides, the court ordered\nthis case is to remain in restricted status pending the Appeal. The Status Conference currently set for Thursday, March 27, 2025 at 1:30\nP.M. in Courtroom 2 - Memphis before Judge Thomas L. Parker is cancelled. (Court Reporter: Catherine Phillips) (smm) (Entered:\n03/21/2025)\n08/14/2025 242 JUDGMENT of USCA (certified copy) as to Ashley Grayson re 216 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment. UNPUBLISHED OPINION and\nJUDGMENT filed : AFFIRMED. Mandate to issue. (jae) (Entered: 08/14/2025)\n09/23/2025 243 MANDATE of USCA (certified copy) as to Ashley Grayson. MANDATE ISSUED with no costs taxed. (cmm) (Entered: 09/23/2025)\n01/05/2026 244 MOTION to Unseal Document ECF 87 and for ECF Access to Documents 110, 213, and 231 by Ashley Grayson. (Turkel, Russell)\n(Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/05/2026 245 DEFICIENCY NOTICE: Pursuant to Rule 49 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, document 244 MOTION to Unseal Document\nECF 87 and for ECF Access to Documents 110, 213, and 231 filed by Ashley Grayson has been filed. However, the following deficiency\nhas been found: The court will make a ruling on the motion to unseal docket entry 87, but if you wish to get copies of docket entries 110,\n213 and 231, you must submit \"sealed document request\"which is found under \"court events - other events- sealed document request\" If\nyou are the attorney of record, these documents can be provided to you. Please refer to the ECF User Manual and ECF Policies and\nProcedures. The filer has one business day to correct the deficiency. (jae) (Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/05/2026 246 *** Sealed document request for (document(s): 110, 213, 231)\n\nDeliver via USPS Mail - 15455 Dallas Parkway, Suite 540, Addison, Texas 75001\n(Turkel, Russell) (Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/05/2026 247 *** Sealed document response for (document(s): 246 *** Sealed document request for (document(s): 110, 213, 231). Document 110 is not\navailable for you are not attorney of record, Document 213 is the sealed judgment and the difference from this and the redacted judgment\nis the Judge's wet signature. Document 231 is not a sealed document. (cmm) (Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/09/2026 248 *** Sealed document response for (document(s): 246 Sealed Document request 110 is not available for you are not the attorney of record.\n*** Sealed document request for (document(s): 110, 213, 231)\n\nDeliver via USPS Mail - 15455 Dallas Parkway, Suite 540, Addison, Texas 75001\n\n(Turkel, Russell) ).\n\nDocument(s) are being physically mailed to the requested address via Paper Printout.\n\n(cmm) (Entered: 01/09/2026)\n01/12/2026 249 ORDER granting 244 Motion to Unseal ECF No. 87 as to Ashley Grayson (1). Signed by Judge Thomas L. Parker on 1/12/2026. (Parker,\nThomas) (Entered: 01/12/2026)\n01/21/2026 250 U.S. Supreme Court notice filed regarding a petition for a writ of certiorari filed by Appellant Ashley Grayson. Supreme Court Case\nNo:25-851, 01/14/2026. (cmm) (Entered: 01/21/2026)\n04/13/2026 251 MOTION to Unseal Document proposed order submitted by United States of America as to Ashley Grayson. (Phillips, Bryce) (Entered:\n04/13